---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Ui.astro';
---

<Base title="Surfaces">
  <h1>Surfaces</h1>
  <p>
    Structure is printed, not floated: panels are 2px ink rules, the table is
    the ledger, dividers are rules with fixed meanings, disclosures are
    programme notes, and tabs are departments on a rule.
  </p>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>PANEL</h2>
    <p>
      A <code>.mk-card</code> is a panel — a 2px ink rule around an inset
      fill. <code>--sunken</code> drops to a quiet 1px tan hairline for
      asides; <code>--flush</code> removes the padding so framed art meets
      the rule edge to edge.
    </p>
    <div class="mk-card mk-card--sunken">
      <strong>From the wings</strong>
      <p style="margin: var(--mk-space-xxs) 0 0; color: var(--mk-color-text-muted);">
        The quiet panel — a hairline aside that does not compete with boxed
        content.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mk-card mk-card--flush" style="margin-top: var(--mk-space-md); max-width: 18rem;">
      <img
        src={(import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/') + 'art/scene-config-water.jpg').replace(/\/+/g, '/')}
        alt="Wilson watering the config while Ake watches with alarm"
        style="width: 100%; display: block;"
      />
      <div style="padding: var(--mk-panel-pad);">
        <strong>The water is the config</strong>
        <p style="margin: 2px 0 0; color: var(--mk-color-text-muted); font-style: italic;">change the water, not the fish</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;div class="mk-card"&gt;
  &lt;div class="mk-card mk-card--sunken"&gt;A quiet aside&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="mk-card mk-card--flush"&gt;&lt;img …&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>THE LEDGER</h2>
    <p>
      Typewriter caps over a 2px ink rule, Goudy figures on hairline rows,
      and a 3px double rule closing the account in <code>tfoot</code>.
      Numeric cells take <code>__num</code>; wrap the whole book in
      <code>.mk-table-wrap</code> so it scrolls inside its own rules.
    </p>
    <div class="mk-table-wrap">
      <table class="mk-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Act</th>
            <th scope="col" class="mk-table__num">Nights</th>
            <th scope="col" class="mk-table__num">Receipts</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Tim Taylor · More Power</td>
            <td class="mk-table__num">12</td>
            <td class="mk-table__num">$1,240.50</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Wilson · Over the Fence</td>
            <td class="mk-table__num">8</td>
            <td class="mk-table__num">$612.00</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Al Borland &amp; His Flannel Revue</td>
            <td class="mk-table__num">5</td>
            <td class="mk-table__num">$301.25</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
        <tfoot>
          <tr>
            <td>IN TOTAL</td>
            <td class="mk-table__num">25</td>
            <td class="mk-table__num">$2,153.75</td>
          </tr>
        </tfoot>
      </table>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;div class="mk-table-wrap"&gt;
  &lt;table class="mk-table"&gt;
    &lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;
      &lt;th scope="col"&gt;Act&lt;/th&gt;
      &lt;th scope="col" class="mk-table__num"&gt;Receipts&lt;/th&gt;
    &lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;
    &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;
      &lt;td&gt;Tim Taylor · More Power&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;td class="mk-table__num"&gt;$1,240.50&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/tbody&gt;
    &lt;tfoot&gt;&lt;tr&gt;
      &lt;td&gt;IN TOTAL&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;td class="mk-table__num"&gt;$2,153.75&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/tfoot&gt;
  &lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>PRINTED RULES</h2>
    <p>
      Rules do the dividing, and each weight has a fixed meaning. Pick the
      rule for what the break means, not for taste. The accent rule spends
      the ochre ration — use it once, if at all.
    </p>
    <p class="rule-note">default · 1px tan — a minor division</p>
    <hr class="mk-divider" />
    <p class="rule-note">--thick · 2px ink — a department underline</p>
    <hr class="mk-divider mk-divider--thick" />
    <p class="rule-note">--double · 4px double — a major section break</p>
    <hr class="mk-divider mk-divider--double" />
    <p class="rule-note">--double-thin · 3px double — the footer break</p>
    <hr class="mk-divider mk-divider--double-thin" />
    <p class="rule-note">--dash · nothing is printed here yet</p>
    <hr class="mk-divider mk-divider--dash" />
    <p class="rule-note">--accent · the ochre rule — rationed</p>
    <hr class="mk-divider mk-divider--accent" />
    <p class="rule-note">--label · a typewriter slug flanked by hairlines</p>
    <div class="mk-divider mk-divider--label"><span>intermission</span></div>
    <pre><code>&lt;hr class="mk-divider" /&gt;
&lt;hr class="mk-divider mk-divider--double" /&gt;
&lt;div class="mk-divider mk-divider--label"&gt;&lt;span&gt;intermission&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>PROGRAMME NOTES</h2>
    <p>
      Native <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> between hairline rules. The marker
      is a typewriter + that becomes &minus; when the note is open — the
      glyph swaps instantly, like set type.
    </p>
    <details class="mk-disclosure">
      <summary>A NOTE ON THE PYROTECHNICS</summary>
      <div class="mk-disclosure__body">
        The management wishes to assure patrons that the flames in Act II are
        entirely intentional, and that Mr. Borland stands in the wings with
        the extinguisher as always.
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="mk-disclosure" open>
      <summary>ON THE MATTER OF THE FENCE</summary>
      <div class="mk-disclosure__body">
        Mr. Wilson appears by arrangement with his garden, and is seen only
        to the brim of his hat. Add the <code>open</code> attribute to unfold
        a note on load.
      </div>
    </details>
    <pre><code>&lt;details class="mk-disclosure"&gt;
  &lt;summary&gt;A NOTE ON THE PYROTECHNICS&lt;/summary&gt;
  &lt;div class="mk-disclosure__body"&gt;…&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/details&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>DEPARTMENTS</h2>
    <p>
      Tabs are departments on a 2px ink rule; the current department
      overprints it with its own ink underline. Selection answers to
      <code>aria-selected</code>, <code>aria-current</code>, or
      <code>--active</code> — the styling hook is the semantics. Tabs wrap
      rather than overflow the rule.
    </p>
    <div class="mk-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Departments of the house">
      <button class="mk-tabs__tab" role="tab" aria-selected="true">Stage</button>
      <button class="mk-tabs__tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Carpentry</button>
      <button class="mk-tabs__tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Wardrobe</button>
      <button class="mk-tabs__tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Front of house</button>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;div class="mk-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Departments"&gt;
  &lt;button class="mk-tabs__tab" role="tab" aria-selected="true"&gt;Stage&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;button class="mk-tabs__tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false"&gt;Carpentry&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <style>
    .rule-note {
      margin: var(--mk-space-md) 0 0;
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: var(--mk-size-mono-xs);
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      color: var(--mk-color-text-muted);
    }

    /* Tighten the demo rules so the meanings read as a chart. */
    .rule-note + .mk-divider {
      margin: var(--mk-space-xs) 0 0;
    }

    section.mk-card + section.mk-card {
      margin-top: var(--mk-space-2xl);
    }

    pre {
      margin-top: var(--mk-space-md);
      padding: 12px 14px;
      background: var(--mk-color-plate);
      border: var(--mk-rule-hair);
      border-left: var(--mk-rule-thick);
      color: var(--mk-color-heading);
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: var(--mk-size-mono-sm);
      line-height: 1.6;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }

    code {
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: 0.86em;
      background: var(--mk-color-plate);
      border: var(--mk-rule-hair);
      color: var(--mk-color-heading);
      padding: 1px 5px 0;
    }

    pre code {
      background: none;
      border: 0;
      padding: 0;
      font-size: inherit;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
